{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a7c3e8d1-4b2f-4e91-9c6a-delivery-rca-001",
    "name": "Delivery Root-Cause Analyzer",
    "description": "Tests the local Spring Boot root-cause API (Java 17).\n\n**Before you start:** `mvn spring-boot:run` and wait until Tomcat is on port 8080.\n\nImport this collection **and** `local.postman_environment.json`, then select environment **Delivery RCA — local**.\n\nWalk through folders top to bottom. Each use-case request matches one assignment question.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Catalog",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Meta — cities, warehouses, demo hints",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/meta",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "meta"]
            },
            "description": "Sanity check that the app loaded CSVs. Expect `orders: 10000`, `asOfDate: 2025-09-12`, city list, and `demoHints`.\n\nUse this to pick other `clientId` / `warehouseId` values for later requests."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Loaded 10000 orders', () => pm.expect(j.orders).to.eql(10000));",
                  "pm.test('Has cities and demoHints', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(j.cities).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(j.demoHints).to.have.property('cityX');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Run all 6 demo use cases at once",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/insights/demo",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "insights", "demo"]
            },
            "description": "Returns a JSON object with six reports:\n- `1_city_yesterday`\n- `2_client_week`\n- `3_warehouse_b_august`\n- `4_city_compare`\n- `5_festival`\n- `6_onboard_client_y`\n\nGood first demo in a video: one call, six narratives."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "['1_city_yesterday','2_client_week','3_warehouse_b_august','4_city_compare','5_festival','6_onboard_client_y'].forEach(k => {",
                  "  pm.test(k + ' has narrative', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(j[k]).to.exist;",
                  "    pm.expect(j[k].narrative).to.be.a('string').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "  });",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "0b. AI natural language",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Ask — Why delayed in New Delhi yesterday?",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/insights/ask?q=Why were deliveries delayed in New Delhi yesterday?",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "insights", "ask"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "q", "value": "Why were deliveries delayed in New Delhi yesterday?" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "AI router maps the sentence to CITY_DELAYS, then the insight engine runs, then the LLM writes the briefing if CURSOR_API_KEY is set.\n\nLook at `intent`, `report.aiGenerated`, `report.narrative`, `report.ruleBasedNarrative`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Has intent and report', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(j.intent).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(j.report.narrative).to.be.a('string').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Ask POST — Client Y 20000 extra orders",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"question\": \"If we onboard Client Y with about 20000 extra monthly orders, what new failure risks should we expect?\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/insights/ask",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "insights", "ask"]
            },
            "description": "Should route to CAPACITY_RISK. With an API key, `report.aiGenerated` is true."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Ask — Warehouse B in August",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/insights/ask?q=Explain the top reasons for delivery failures linked to Warehouse B in August",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "insights", "ask"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "q", "value": "Explain the top reasons for delivery failures linked to Warehouse B in August" }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Sample use cases",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1 — Why were deliveries delayed in City X yesterday?",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/insights/city-delays?city=New Delhi&date=2025-01-24",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "insights", "city-delays"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "city", "value": "New Delhi", "description": "City X. Also try: Ahmedabad, Chennai, Bengaluru, Pune" },
                { "key": "date", "value": "2025-01-24", "description": "Operational 'yesterday' — busiest problem day in the CSV (not OS clock)" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Assignment Q1.** Dataset calendar is Jan–Sep 2025, so 'yesterday' is **2025-01-24** in New Delhi (highest problem city-day).\n\n**What to look for**\n- `metrics.orders` around 27\n- `metrics.problems` and `problemRate`\n- `causes[]` ranked (weather, stockout, warehouse, address, traffic)\n- `narrative` paragraph\n- `recommendations[]`\n- `sampleOrderIds`\n\n**Alternate:** `city=Ahmedabad&date=2025-07-15`"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Has insight fields', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(j.title).to.include('City');",
                  "  pm.expect(j.metrics.orders).to.be.above(0);",
                  "  pm.expect(j.narrative).to.include('New Delhi');",
                  "  pm.expect(j.recommendations).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2 — Why did Client X's orders fail last week?",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/insights/client-failures?clientId=409&from=2025-08-10&to=2025-08-16",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "insights", "client-failures"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "clientId", "value": "409", "description": "Client X = Bath, Bhatt and Gulati" },
                { "key": "from", "value": "2025-08-10" },
                { "key": "to", "value": "2025-08-16" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Assignment Q2.** Client **409** (Bath, Bhatt and Gulati) in a week that actually has failed/returned orders.\n\n**What to look for**\n- Scope contains the client name\n- Small slice (~3 orders) with 100% problem rate — still explains weather / warehouse / breakdown\n\n**Alternate client:** `clientId=390` (Sha and Sons) with a wider range, e.g. `from=2025-05-01&to=2025-05-31`"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Client 409 named in scope', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(j.scope).to.match(/409/);",
                  "  pm.expect(j.metrics.orders).to.be.at.least(1);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "3 — Top failure reasons for Warehouse B in August",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/insights/warehouse-failures?warehouseId=2&yearMonth=2025-08",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "insights", "warehouse-failures"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "warehouseId", "value": "2", "description": "Warehouse B = Warehouse 2, Pune" },
                { "key": "yearMonth", "value": "2025-08", "description": "ISO year-month" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Assignment Q3.** `warehouseId=2` is aliased as **Warehouse B** (Pune).\n\n**What to look for**\n- Title/scope mentions Warehouse B / Warehouse 2\n- Causes include warehouse delay, system issue, slow packing, stockout\n- `yearMonth` format must be `YYYY-MM` (not `08-2025`)"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Warehouse B / Pune', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(j.scope).to.match(/Warehouse 2|Warehouse B|Pune/i);",
                  "  pm.expect(j.metrics.orders).to.be.above(0);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "4 — Compare City A vs City B last month",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/insights/city-compare?cityA=New Delhi&cityB=Ahmedabad&yearMonth=2025-08",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "insights", "city-compare"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "cityA", "value": "New Delhi" },
                { "key": "cityB", "value": "Ahmedabad" },
                { "key": "yearMonth", "value": "2025-08" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Assignment Q4.** Side-by-side New Delhi vs Ahmedabad for August 2025.\n\n**What to look for**\n- Metrics for both cities (`New Delhi orders`, `Ahmedabad problem rate`, top cause each)\n- Narrative that says whether the **primary cause differs**\n- Ranked causes tagged with the city name in `evidenceNote`\n\n**Alternate:** `cityA=Chennai&cityB=Bengaluru&yearMonth=2025-07`"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Both cities in metrics', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(j.metrics).to.have.property('New Delhi orders');",
                  "  pm.expect(j.metrics).to.have.property('Ahmedabad orders');",
                  "  pm.expect(j.narrative).to.include('New Delhi');",
                  "  pm.expect(j.narrative).to.include('Ahmedabad');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "5 — Festival period causes and how to prepare",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/insights/festival?from=2025-01-01&to=2025-09-12",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "insights", "festival"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "from", "value": "2025-01-01" },
                { "key": "to", "value": "2025-09-12" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Assignment Q5.** Festival is a flag on `external_factors.event_type`, not a Diwali calendar window.\n\n**What to look for**\n- `festivalOrders` vs `baselineOrders`\n- `festivalProblemRate` vs `baselineProblemRate` (in this CSV they are close — that is expected)\n- Recommendations include a festival control-tower / surge roster"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Festival vs baseline metrics', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(j.metrics.festivalOrders).to.be.above(0);",
                  "  pm.expect(j.metrics.baselineOrders).to.be.above(0);",
                  "  pm.expect(j.narrative).to.match(/Festival/i);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "6 — Onboard Client Y with ~20,000 extra monthly orders",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/insights/capacity-risk?similarClientId=118&extraMonthlyOrders=20000",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "insights", "capacity-risk"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "similarClientId", "value": "118", "description": "Proxy Client Y = Atwal-Dhawan" },
                { "key": "extraMonthlyOrders", "value": "20000" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Assignment Q6.** What-if: add 20k monthly orders using client **118** Atwal-Dhawan as the failure-mix proxy.\n\n**What to look for**\n- `volumeIncreaseVsCurrentMonthly` around 18x\n- `expectedExtraProblemShipmentsPerMonth`\n- Narrative that this is a network redesign, not a small onboard\n- Mitigations: phase volume, extra pack lines in New Delhi\n\n**Alternate:** `extraMonthlyOrders=5000` to see a smaller surge story."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Capacity what-if fields', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(j.metrics.expectedExtraProblemShipmentsPerMonth).to.exist;",
                  "  pm.expect(j.narrative).to.match(/20000|20,000|20k/i);",
                  "  pm.expect(j.recommendations.length).to.be.at.least(2);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
